{#
  VIP badge — a small fixed disc in the bottom-right corner for a visitor who came
  in through /vip/{slug}: a crown over the word VIP. Press it and a greeting unfolds
  to its left — "Great to have you here, Marcus" — then tucks itself away again
  (see vip.js). On every page, for as long as the cookie resolves to a live entry
  (see services\Vip); nothing at all for anyone else.

  Fixed, and rendered OUTSIDE body > .b-wrap (see _layouts/page): the page warps
  transform the wrap, and a fixed element inside a transformed ancestor stops
  being fixed.

  data-vip carries the uid so vip.js can notice the door changing hands (a second
  VIP link on the same browser) and start the conversation afresh.
#}
{% set vipService = craft.app.getModule('jonson').vip %}
{% set vip = vipService.current() %}
{% if vip %}
<div class="c-vip" data-vip="{{ vip.uid }}">
    <p class="c-vip__greeting" id="vip-greeting" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="c-vip__greeting-lead">{{ vipService.personalise('Great to have you here', vip) }}</span>
        <span class="c-vip__greeting-sub">As a VIP, expect a tailored experience</span>
    </p>
    <button class="c-vip__disc" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="vip-greeting" aria-label="VIP: {{ vip.title }}" data-vip-disc>
        {# A crown over the word — inline, as the site's other small marks are (the
           ask bar's sparkles, the footer's arrows), so it takes currentColor. #}
        <svg class="c-vip__crown" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M2.5 7.5 7 11.5 12 4l5 7.5 4.5-4-2 10H4.5l-2-10Zm2.3 12.5h14.4a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v.5a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4.8a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V21a1 1 0 0 1 1-1Z"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="c-vip__tag" aria-hidden="true">VIP</span>
    </button>
</div>
{% endif %}
